\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S32}{\ignorespaces Transition-dataset schema for the surrogate models. Every field of a training tuple $(s_t,a_t,d_t,s_{t+1})$ is tagged by role: \textbf  {M} BOPTEST measurement, \textbf  {X} exogenous disturbance, \textbf  {D} derived feature, \textbf  {A} control action, \textbf  {T} regression target. In a recursive rollout the predicted targets update the physical-state block of the next observation ($\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle T$}\mathaccent "0362{T}_{\mathrm  {zone},t+1}=T_{\mathrm  {zone},t}+\Delta \setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle T$}\mathaccent "0362{T}_{\mathrm  {zone},t+1}$, power, previous action), while exogenous, forecast, and time fields advance from the disturbance stream; the policy then emits $a_{t+1}$ and the map $f_\theta $ is re-applied.}}{23}{table.caption.63}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:transition-schema}{{S32}{23}{Transition-dataset schema for the surrogate models. Every field of a training tuple $(s_t,a_t,d_t,s_{t+1})$ is tagged by role: \textbf {M} BOPTEST measurement, \textbf {X} exogenous disturbance, \textbf {D} derived feature, \textbf {A} control action, \textbf {T} regression target. In a recursive rollout the predicted targets update the physical-state block of the next observation ($\widehat {T}_{\mathrm {zone},t+1}=T_{\mathrm {zone},t}+\Delta \widehat {T}_{\mathrm {zone},t+1}$, power, previous action), while exogenous, forecast, and time fields advance from the disturbance stream; the policy then emits $a_{t+1}$ and the map $f_\theta $ is re-applied}{table.caption.63}{}}
